  "notes": "Source: official University of Cincinnati eCurriculum 'Degree Programs' guide 10739, the UC-published term-by-term plan of study for the B.S. in Computer Science (program code 20BC-CS-BSCS), College of Engineering and Applied Science, Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, covering entering cohort Fall 2023 through Spring 2028. Manually transcribed from the rendered guide on 2026-09-30. Source URL: https://webapps2.uc.edu/ecurriculum/degreeprograms/home/guide/10739. Degree name ('Bachelor of Science in Computer Science') cross-verified on the CEAS degree page (https://ceas.uc.edu/academics/departments/computer-science/degrees-programs/computer-science-bachelor-of-science.html). catalog_year '2023-2024' is the catalog year of the guide's entering term (Fall 2023). Term structure: the official guide shows 13 terms across 5 years (8 academic terms alternating with 5 required zero-credit co-op rotations; UC engineering degrees follow a five-year co-op model). The degree-tracker pipeline allows at most 12 semesters for a bachelor's plan, so the guide's final two senior-year academic terms (Fall 2027 and Spring 2028) are combined into a single entry here; every course and credit hour is unchanged. Co-op: five required 0-credit co-op rotations (COOP2011, COOP2012, COOP3011, COOP4011, COOP4012) are modeled as required_zero placeholders in their own terms, exactly as the guide shows them. Credit total: the sequence sums to 125 SH with the science elective at its 4-credit minimum (126 at 5 credits); the guide's footer describes this as the 'typical minimum number of credit hours'. Older CEAS curriculum sheets (classes of 2021/2022) stated a 124 SH minimum and used superseded course numbering (e.g. ENED1020/1090/1091, CS2021 Python Programming 2 cr); the eCurriculum guide is the current official sequence, so its own total is used. The three 'General Education course' rows in the terms map to the three requirements in the guide's General Education section (BoK: SCE contemporary-topics breadth; one additional gen-ed course from FA/HP/HU/SS/SCE; BoK distribution from FA/HP/HU/SS). Grade requirements: the guide marks many courses '(C- min)' - these are minimum-grade requirements, not prerequisites, and are recorded here as a note only. Prerequisites: the guide states no prerequisite chains, so none were invented; the plan is self-contained beginning at Calculus I, and external_prereqs is empty. Note: catalog.uc.edu could not be opened directly (network timeout on 2026-09-30); the UC eCurriculum guide, an official UC publication linked from the program's detail page, is the primary source.",
